{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play","id":1504160,"title":"Ever make a unique Path/Discipline that you know will never come into play?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-01T18:42:41-08:00","id":1504160,"title":"Ever make a unique Path/Discipline that you know will never come into play?","content":"As many of you know, I am obsessed with the umbra and Inhabitants and feel that they are criminally underrepresented within VTM. So what did I do? I made a nonsensical and somewhat incoherent Blood Magic path which can affect any and every type of spiritual being. Whether it be a simple flame spirit or even the soul within a living creature's body, it doesn't matter because it can affect them all! I call it &quot;The Others&quot;. Why did I choose to name it that? Absolutely no clue.\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>The Others-</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>The Senses- The practitioners have attuned their senses to the spiritual beings around them and can now speak with spiritual creatures such as ghosts, spirits, demons, astral creatures, and even those that are in inanimate and animate things, such as fire, water, souls in bodies, etc. When this ability is activated, the practitioner will speak in the language the creature they are interacting with is most comfortable with.</b></li> <li><b>Carrot and the Stick- The practitioner can either feed a spiritual being Vitae or harm the being by feeding on it. When feeding, the vampire can choose to satiate their bloodlust or strengthen their willpower. This technique can be used to reward or punish the spirit, and can help a vampire survive when hunting live prey is simply out of the question. When used on the inanimate or animate ones, it will strengthen the attributes if they are fed, or decrease it if they are fed on.</b></li> <li><b>The Summon- The Practitioner can now summon spiritual beings to their side. To do so they need at least rudimentary knowledge on the specific spirit they wish to call, for example one will need to know the appearance and name of a wraith, or the concept of the spirit they wish to summon, such as one of sadness. This power can be used to summon spiritual beings from their physical shells as well but will be more difficult.</b></li> <li><b>The Command- The practitioner can now command spiritual beings to follow their orders. It is best to use \u2018Carrot and Stick\u2019 when using this power as it cements your position as either a terrifying creature who will punish the spiritual being for not following orders properly, or a benevolent person who is willing to reward the summoned being for listening to them. Or one can simply take the \u201cTough, but fair\u201d approach. It can be a bit tricker when using it on those which are within either inanimate, such as spirits of rocks, or animate shells such as souls within the body.</b></li> <li><b>The Binding- The practitioner can now bind spiritual beings to either inanimate or animate objects, creatures, or places. They have also gained the ability to create fretters, fetishes and the like, as well as strengthening those bindings. They can also weaken and free them from their bindings. If done on those that are either inanimate or animate, you can expect many different outcomes. </b></li> </ol><br /> Has anyone else wasted too much time making unique Disciplines/Paths that may never come into play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T19:00:28-08:00","id":1504162,"title":"","content":"Back in my teens and early twenties I ran a Lasombra character from Dark Ages to Modern Nights over about eight years. I took about two dozen self created Combination Disciplines to basically turn my character into Carnage meets Jean Grey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T20:35:36-08:00","id":1504170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504162#post1504162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in my teens and early twenties I ran a Lasombra character from Dark Ages to Modern Nights over about eight years. I took about two dozen self created Combination Disciplines to basically turn my character into Carnage meets Jean Grey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cant even begin to image such a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T01:41:46-08:00","id":1504183,"title":"","content":"Flight, but for people wearing capes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:36:16-08:00","id":1504190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504183#post1504183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flight, but for people wearing capes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There should be more specialized, characterful, obscure and interesting Disciplines or abilities like Flight. It is good and nice that the Disciplines of Temporis, Dementation, and also of course Serpentis definitely make a decent enough impression in regard to encompassing particular concepts and themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T08:26:21-08:00","id":1504204,"title":"","content":"I mostly disagree. In my mind, 50% of inceptor disciplines are really just Protean mutations (I'll lump in serpentis, thanatosis and Viskeratica here). 40% are esper-themed thaumaturgy. 5% is a variation on one of the rarer/bloodline disciplines (Probably feeding from something weird) , and maybe that last 5% is genuinely new and something worth a story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T10:38:29-08:00","id":1504214,"title":"","content":"I made two paths for the ultimate Tremere paper-pusher character I actually got to play for a bit.<br /> <br /> Ars Notoria (based on the art of the same name from the <i>Lesser Key of Solomon</i>)<br /> <br /> 1. Speed-Reading, volume by successes<br /> 2. Eidetic Memory, details by successes<br /> 3. Learn contents of medium by touch, volume by successes<br /> 4. Same, but regardless of language<br /> 5. Same, but with a radius effect instead of touch (aka fun in libraries)<br /> <br /> Bureaucrathurgy (based on the few canon rituals around paperwork)<br /> <br /> 1. Understand filing systems, procedures etc intuitively<br /> 2. Summon a perfectly filled out copy of a form<br /> 3. Mini-dominate through formal letters<br /> 4. Document alchemy (transmute/refine media)<br /> 5. Magically cycle through document iterations (turn first edition works into second, convert an application into an approval etc)<br /> <br /> The second one especially was surprisingly more fun than I expected, and rituals like Expedient Paperwork are really underrated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T11:40:25-08:00","id":1504217,"title":"","content":"I wanted to make Necroscope Wamphyri, and was deeply dissatisfied with Viccissitude. Vic is too powerful in some ways, and too weak in others to duplicate the powers of the Wamphyri. So I came up with my own discipline to duplicate the Wamphyri power more precisely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T13:57:37-08:00","id":1504224,"title":"","content":"I created a mortis/Necromancy path which was lure of the flames but damage varied of how dead you were.<br /> <br /> Humans=bashing<br /> Vampires=lethal<br /> wraiths=aggravated<br /> <br /> Flames where blue and had an elderich vibr<br /> <br /> was mostly something showy for a big shot cappadocians and harbingers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-02-2023, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T01:53:54-08:00","id":1504249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504224#post1504224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I created a mortis/Necromancy path which was lure of the flames but damage varied of how dead you were.<br /> <br /> Humans=bashing<br /> Vampires=lethal<br /> wraiths=aggravated<br /> <br /> Flames where blue and had an elderich vibr<br /> <br /> was mostly something showy for a big shot cappadocians and harbingers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me<br /> I did make a lure of flames necromancy path that only worked on ghosts, and could only be seen by ghosts. The flame was white, since I think I read something about barrowfire in wraith being white. But I did actually use this in game with an NPC and I think a player learned a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-03-2023, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T03:31:43-08:00","id":1504252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504217#post1504217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to make Necroscope Wamphyri, and was deeply dissatisfied with Viccissitude. Vic is too powerful in some ways, and too weak in others to duplicate the powers of the Wamphyri. So I came up with my own discipline to duplicate the Wamphyri power more precisely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, have you shared the writeup anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T06:32:42-08:00","id":1504258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504204#post1504204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly disagree. In my mind, 50% of inceptor disciplines are really just Protean mutations (I'll lump in serpentis, thanatosis and Viskeratica here). 40% are esper-themed thaumaturgy. 5% is a variation on one of the rarer/bloodline disciplines (Probably feeding from something weird) , and maybe that last 5% is genuinely new and something worth a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean variants and also the various Protean additional and alternate powers / abilities are very nice and interesting. There are also the Protean powers which are known, cherished, developed, and used by Gangrel Kindred who are the aqua-themed \\ water-dwelling Mariners.<br /> <br /> Which of the main / standard Blood Magic Paths (and maybe also Rituals) would you consider or categorize as esper-themed, assuming relatively normal and straightforward criteria?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T06:44:34-08:00","id":1504260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504258#post1504258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which of the main / standard Blood Magic Paths (and maybe also Rituals) would you consider or categorize as esper-themed, assuming relatively normal and straightforward criteria?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of paths do have potential to be done under an Esper (Psychic might be a better word) paradigm, especially simple paths like movement of the mind or lure of flames, but I can also see potential in most other paths too (Look daddy, I can talk to trees/Inanimate objects!) <br /> <br /> Rituals on the otherhand, are going to be quite barebones. Maybe they'll stick to simple things like healing crystals or that power that jams technology, or maybe their &quot;psychic power&quot; will guide them to more complex rituals. <br /> <br /> In any case, I think someone who stumbles in on thaumaturgy thinking they're psychic is going to have a difficult time progressing in the practice. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T11:34:17-08:00","id":1504281,"title":"","content":"Sadly no as I'm not creative enough to create whole disciplines out of the ether and I just stick with trying to create amalgam/devotions powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T15:27:53-08:00","id":1504294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1504160-ever-make-a-unique-path-discipline-that-you-know-will-never-come-into-play?p=1504252#post1504252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, have you shared the writeup anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, but, irrc, it was basically the first few levels of Requiem Protean and then became Path of Conjuring mechanics adapted to make biological machinery when you have a restrained victim and lots of time in a laboratory.<br /> <br /> The Wamphyri have modest shapeshifting ability, and the ability to make complex, powerful biomachinery when they have restrained victims and lots of laboratory time, so it was just a matter of adapting Protean and Path of Conjuring mechanics to simulate this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T23:54:05-08:00","id":1504336,"title":"","content":"I have a slight aversion to unique Disciplines so I'm afraid I haven't yet found a concept I thought solid enough to actually make into a Discipline.<br /> <br /> But you never know, maybe I will make one someday in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}